\section{Data}{

Data should follow the column naming of the PBTM template (see
\link{pbtm_columns}): one row per observation, with the cumulative time
(\code{CumTime}), the cumulative germinated fraction (\code{CumFraction}, 0-1), and the
treatment columns required by the model (e.g. \code{GermTemp} for thermal time).
Use \code{cols} to map differently named columns onto the template names.

Rate models (hydropriming and hydrothermal priming) are fit to germination
rates. Pass the raw time-course data (which also needs a \code{TrtID} column) and
the rates are computed with \code{\link[=germ_speed]{germ_speed()}} at the fraction given by \code{speed};
alternatively, pass a data frame that already has a \code{GR} column.
