For cumulative (\code{"cdf"}) models, \code{subpops > 1} fits a mixture of distinct
seed subpopulations, each with its own copy of the model parameters, combined
with mixing weights that sum to one. Parameters of subpopulation \code{j} get the
suffix \code{j} (e.g. \code{t_b1}, \code{t_b2}) and the free mixing fractions are named
