several perturbed starting values (\code{restarts}) and the best fit by AIC is
kept. \code{subpops = "auto"} fits 1 to \code{max_subpops} subpopulations and keeps
the one with the lowest AIC. Mixture fits are often \emph{equifinal} (different
parameter sets fit almost equally well), so treat the component estimates
with caution; see \code{vignette("subpopulations", package = "pbtm")}.
